# Documentation sync (mandatory)

When a change affects how developers or agents use the codebase, update the
matching documentation and rules in the **same task** — do not leave stale names,
paths, or examples.

## Trigger — update docs when you

- Rename, merge, or remove a public export (component, hook, route, constant, env field)
- Change root wiring (`src/app/**/layout.tsx`, providers, `proxy.ts`)
- Add or change a mandatory pattern (error boundaries, auth, documents, env)
- Edit an always-on agent rule (`.cursor/rules/*.mdc`)

## Where to update

| Topic | Primary doc |
| ----- | ----------- |
| Error boundaries, documents, quality gates | `doc/guides/error-handling-and-documents.md` |
| Folder structure, naming, imports | `doc/guides/folder-structure.md`, `doc/guides/conventions.md` |
| AI rules and skills | `doc/guides/ai-agents-skills-and-rules.md`, `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` |
| Documented components | `doc/components/*.md` |
| Notable product or infra changes | `CHANGELOG.md` → `[Unreleased]` |

## How

1. Grep `doc/`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `.cursor/rules/`, `.devin/rules/`, and `AGENTS.md` for the old symbol or path.
2. Replace with the new API; refresh code samples to match current imports and props.
3. When consolidating duplicates, document the single component/API and remove obsolete sections.
4. Mirror rule edits to `.devin/rules/` with `pnpm agent:sync` (same basename).

Do **not** create new doc files unless the user asked or no existing guide section fits.
